{"id":"galatians","links":[{"id":"q27","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"galatians","c":3,"v":8},"b":{"book":"genesis","c":12,"v":3},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"Galatians says “All nations will be blessed through you”; Genesis says “all the families of the earth will be blessed through you.”"},{"id":"q29","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"galatians","c":3,"v":16},"b":{"book":"genesis","c":13,"v":15},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"Galatians says the promises were spoken to Abraham “and to your seed,” meaning One; Genesis says the land goes “to you and your offspring forever.”"},{"id":"q35","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"galatians","c":3,"v":6},"b":{"book":"genesis","c":15,"v":6},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"Galatians repeats “Abraham believed God, and it was credited to him as righteousness”; Genesis says Abram believed the LORD."},{"id":"q40","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"galatians","c":3,"v":16},"b":{"book":"genesis","c":17,"v":7},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"Galatians stresses “and to your seed” rather than seeds; Genesis speaks of a covenant between “Me and you and your descendants after you.”"},{"id":"q44","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"galatians","c":4,"v":30},"b":{"book":"genesis","c":21,"v":10},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"Galatians repeats “Expel the slave woman and her son”; Genesis has these words spoken to Abraham, about the slave woman’s son and Isaac."},{"id":"q151","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"galatians","c":3,"v":12},"b":{"book":"leviticus","c":18,"v":5},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"Galatians repeats “The man who does these things will live by them”; Leviticus has the same words after “Keep My statutes.”"},{"id":"q161","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"galatians","c":5,"v":14},"b":{"book":"leviticus","c":19,"v":18},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"Galatians repeats “Love your neighbor as yourself” as a single decree for the entire law; Leviticus has the same words."},{"id":"q226","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"galatians","c":3,"v":13},"b":{"book":"deuteronomy","c":21,"v":23},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"Galatians repeats “who is hung on a tree” and calls that person cursed; Deuteronomy says such a person “is under God’s curse.”"},{"id":"q236","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"galatians","c":3,"v":10},"b":{"book":"deuteronomy","c":27,"v":26},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"Galatians and Deuteronomy both pronounce a curse on whoever does not keep the law: “Cursed is everyone,” in Galatians; “Cursed is he,” in Deuteronomy."},{"id":"q441","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"galatians","c":2,"v":16},"b":{"book":"psalms","c":143,"v":2},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"Galatians says “by works of the law no one will be justified”; Psalms says “no one alive is righteous before You”."},{"id":"q564","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"galatians","c":1,"v":15},"b":{"book":"isaiah","c":49,"v":1},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"Galatians says God “set me apart from my mother’s womb”; Isaiah says “The LORD called Me from the womb.”"},{"id":"q586","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"galatians","c":4,"v":27},"b":{"book":"isaiah","c":54,"v":1},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"Galatians repeats Isaiah’s call to “O barren woman, who bears no children,” and to break forth and cry aloud."},{"id":"q617","type":"quotation","